 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize Sean Ralston to take the competitive civil service\nexamination and be placed on the eligible list for appointment as a full-time\npolice officer",
    "basePrintNo": "S6908",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6908-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6908\n\nSPONSOR: AMEDORE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize Sean Ralston to take the compet-\nitive civil service examination and be placed on the eligible list for\nappointment as a full-time police officer\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes Sean Ralston to take the competitive exam for full-time\npolice officer and be placed on the eligible list for such position.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Authorizes Sean Ralston to sit for the civil service exam and\nbe placed on the eligibility list for full-time police officer.\n\nSection 2. Sean Ralston is subject to the merit and fitness provisions\nof the civil service law applicable to full-time officers\n\nSection 3. This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder the Civil Service Law, as prescribed under Section 58, no individ-\nual may take the civil service examination, nor be eligible for a civil\nservice appointment as a police officer, at the age of 35 or older. Due\nto this limitation, the village of Altamont has requested legislation to\npermit one of their part-time officers, Sean Ralston, to be eligible to\ntake the civil service examination since he is currently older than 35\nyears old.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS TO STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
